{{!--
  Header toolbar (see GH issue #7), aligned to the same DS grid container as
  the breadcrumb toolbar (grid-layout/grid-layout.css, vendored via
  src/css/ids-components.yml): `.ids-grid-layout--with-margin` gives the
  correct per-breakpoint gutter (16/32/56/64px). Both halves carry
  `--span-6` (half of the grid's 12 columns at s and up) *and* `--span-xs-3`
  (half of its 6 columns at xs) so the row never stacks at any breakpoint —
  see GH-8's own discussion for why a bare `--span-6` alone would.

  GH-77: the search trigger lives in the *actions* group, not the left one —
  first child there, ahead of the version tag/repo link/theme toggle — so it
  reads right-aligned with the rest of that cluster (`.header-toolbar__actions`'s
  own `justify-content: flex-end`, unchanged) at every breakpoint instead of
  sitting apart from it. It changes shape per breakpoint (header.css), all in
  one markup tree:
  - l/m: full trigger — icon, "Search" label, ⌘K chip.
  - s: icon + "Search" label, chip drops.
  - xs: hidden outright — GH-68 (S4)'s floating button (search-dialog.hbs)
    is the only trigger there, untouched by this.

  The menu toggle (see GH issue #8): `hidden` until src/js/01-nav.ts wires
  it up, same reasoning as theme-toggle.hbs — a control with no handler
  must not render.

  GH-67 (S3): the trigger is wired up by src/js/12-search.ts, which also adds
  its `aria-haspopup`/`aria-controls` (a popup this button can't yet open
  shouldn't advertise one, so those are set from script alongside the
  handler that makes them true, not authored here). Guarded by
  `page.componentVersion.searchIndex` — antora-extensions/lib/search-index.js
  only sets that attribute when the component version produced at least one
  record, so a version with nothing to search gets no trigger at all rather
  than one that opens onto a permanently-empty dialog. The ⌘K chip always
  renders the Apple glyph server-side (no way to detect the platform without
  JS) — 12-search.ts corrects it to "Ctrl K" client-side where needed.
  Showing the wrong modifier to a Linux user for one frame beats a layout
  shift on every load.

  The version tag (page-versions.hbs) is hidden at s/xs — GH-8's Figma
  frames for those breakpoints move it into the side-menu drawer instead
  (see nav.hbs, side-menu.css), it doesn't just disappear. Repo becomes
  icon-only there too, since the
  full "AMIGA FRAMEWORK WEB" + "repo" + theme toggle no longer fits a
  390px bar alongside the menu button — not something Figma specifies, a
  call made for this breakpoint.

  `variant='home'` (GH-18) used to make this partial render an extra leading
  ghost icon ahead of the old dead input, the only difference Figma drew
  between the toolbar's "Home" and "Default" states. The new trigger (GH-66)
  always carries its own leading icon, so that distinction is gone — the
  Home/Default states no longer differ here, and home.hbs no longer passes
  `variant` (see its own history for the prior plumbing, kept in this
  partial's git blame rather than as dead code today).

  The brand link now carries an optional logo (`site.keys.productLogo`/
  `productLogoDark`) ahead of the product name, same dark-swap convention as
  nav-brand.hbs/nav.hbs (`{{#with}}` skips the `<img>` entirely when unset,
  no placeholder mark) — every other spot this bundle shows the mark
  (side-menu, drawer header) already did; the toolbar itself was text-only
  until now.
--}}
<header class="header-toolbar">
  <div class="ids-grid-layout ids-grid-layout--with-margin header-toolbar__grid">
    <div class="ids-grid-layout__item ids-grid-layout__item--span-6 ids-grid-layout__item--span-xs-3 header-toolbar__left">
      <button class="ids-button ids-button--ghost ids-button--icon-only side-menu-toggle" type="button" aria-controls="side-menu" hidden>
        <span class="ids-button__content">
          <span class="ids-button__icon ids-button__icon-icon">{{icon "design" "menu-tab-outlined"}}</span>
        </span>
      </button>
      <a class="header-toolbar__brand" href="{{{relativize (or site.homeUrl page.componentVersion.url)}}}"{{#if page.home}} aria-current="page"{{/if}}>
{{#with site.keys.productLogo}}
        <img class="header-toolbar__logo{{#if @root.site.keys.productLogoDark}} header-toolbar__logo--light{{/if}}" src="{{{relativize this}}}" width="24" height="24" alt="">
{{/with}}
{{#with site.keys.productLogoDark}}
        <img class="header-toolbar__logo header-toolbar__logo--dark" src="{{{relativize this}}}" width="24" height="24" alt="">
{{/with}}
        <span class="header-toolbar__product-name ids-text ids-text--label-l-high">{{or page.component.title site.title}}</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="ids-grid-layout__item ids-grid-layout__item--span-6 ids-grid-layout__item--span-xs-3 header-toolbar__actions">
{{#if page.componentVersion.searchIndex}}
      <button type="button" class="ids-button ids-button--ghost header-toolbar__search-trigger">
        <span class="ids-button__content">
          <span class="ids-button__icon ids-button__icon-icon">{{icon "actions" "search-outlined"}}</span>
          <span class="ids-text ids-text--label-l header-toolbar__search-label">Search</span>
          <kbd class="header-toolbar__search-shortcut" aria-hidden="true">⌘K</kbd>
        </span>
      </button>
{{/if}}
{{> page-versions}}
{{> repo-link}}
{{> theme-toggle}}
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
